    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Charges based on annual Transmission Revenue Requirement as approved by the FERC</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote"/>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Account 409.2</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Balance as of 12/31/2025 was included in CWIP (FERC account 107)</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In its formula rate on file with the Commission, certain non-plant items are not included in rate base.&#160; The value used to update the formula rate has been adjusted to remove amounts related to these items not in rate base.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In its formula rate on file with the Commission, certain non-plant items are not included in rate base.&#160; The value used to update the formula rate has been adjusted to remove amounts related to these items not in rate base.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Land presented as historical cost, which is not depreciated</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">As a result of the placing the Sloan Canyon project in-service, the existing line of 83.45 miles is split between thefollowing:Mead - Sloan, approximately 14 miles and Pahrump - Sloan approximately 72 miles.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Consists of one 230 kV circuits (GridLiance West Owned) and one 138 kV circuits (Valley ElectricAssociation owned). Pahrump 230/138 kV double circuit. The 138 kV conductor is 336 ACRS. The230 kV conductor is 795 ACSR.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">GridLiance Management, LLC ("ManageCo") provides corporate services on an as-needed basis, including but not limited to, corporate oversight, human resources, records management, risk management, and payroll services at cost. The Company allocated indirect costs from ManageCo based on the Company's "Direct Charge" cost allocation methodology which is based on a proportional ratio of direct charges to each affiliate.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Services provided by affiliated companies may include executive &amp; governance, finance &amp; accounting, corporate communications, legal, corporate real estate, human resources, payroll, security, internal audit, information management operations and maintenance, and license fees. Services are allocated to affiliates using specific drivers such as headcount or number of workstations. If cost cannot be attributed, the services are allocated using the Massachusetts Formula.</link:footnote>
